Abstract = {A new species of Gonolobus from northwestern Mexico with green and
   barbate corollas is described here. Gonolobus naturalistae is
   morphologically similar to G. barbatus, G. pectinatus, and G. sororius
   but differs in corolla and corona morphology and distribution.
   Descriptions, illustrations, morphological comparisons, and geographic
   distribution maps of these species, as well as their conservation
   status, are provided. This discovery highlights Mexico as a center of
   diversity for the genus, with around 40 species recorded, and highlights
   its endemism, with 48.7\% of the species occurring in the country.},
