Volume = {45},
Number = {3},
Pages = {753-779},
Month = {SEP},
Abstract = {We describe and compare the exochorion of three species of Heliconiinae
   from Mexico (Euptoieta hegesia meridiania, Agraulis vanillae incarnata,
   and Laparus doris viridis) with other previously published species from
   southern Brazil. The comparison emphasizes the main exochorionic
   characters such as `ornamentation', micropylar, perimicropylar, and
   transition zones differentiation, as well as equatorial and basal
   reticules. We used the staining technique and scanning electron
   microscope. Structural differences are recognized in two of the
   Heliconiinae tribes, being characteristic in Argynnini its truncated
   conical shape, the presence of two reticules (supra and
   infra-equatorial), and perhaps keels in the apex; while Heliconiini has
   oblong ellipsoidal shapes and a rectangular grid with some penta or
   hexagonal polygons in the apical region. Morphology in Acraeini, the
   possible implications of chorionic morphology in the systematics of
   Heliconiinae, and the characters in some species are briefly discussed.
   Sheets and diagrams are included/presented for clear visualization of
   the structures and areas described in the chorion of Argynnini and
   Heliconiini.},
