Abstract = {Good's Theorem for regular continued fraction states that the set of
   real numbers {[}a(0);a(1),a(2),...] such that lim(n ->infinity) a(n) =
   infinity has Hausdorff dimension 1/2. We show an analogous result for
   the complex plane and Hurwitz Continued Fractions: the set of complex
   numbers whose Hurwitz Continued fraction {[}a(0);a(1),a(2),...]satisfies
   lim(n ->infinity) vertical bar a(n)vertical bar= infinity has Hausdorff
   dimension 1, half of the ambient space's dimension.},
