Abstract = {LetGbe a simplen-vertex graph andcbe a coloring ofE(G)withncolors, where
   each color class has size at least 2. We prove that(G,c)contains a
   rainbow cycle of length at most left ceiling n2 right ceiling , which is
   best possible. Our result settles a special case of a strengthening of
   the Caccetta-Haggkvist conjecture, due to Aharoni. We also show that the
   matroid generalization of our main result also holds for cographic
   matroids, but fails for binary matroids.},
