Pages = {627-648},
Abstract = {According to records available in the literature, 380 species of fungi
   and fungus-like organisms are known for the state of Quintana Roo on the
   Yucatan Peninsula of Mexico. We carried out mycological surveys in this
   state, following the classical methods for collecting, describing, and
   curating macrofungi. As a result of our research, 21 species are
   recorded for the first time for Quintana Roo, and Amanita arenicola O.
   K. Milller \& Lodge, Inocybe xerophytica Pegler, and Russula
   cremeolilacina Pegler are recorded for the first time for Mexico. The
   distinctive characteristics and photographs are provided for the new
   records. As a result of this study, 401 species of macrofungi are known
   for Quintana Roo.},
